{"id":"effect-9a4aa291-3bce-5286-90b4-f8a2618922ac","sessionId":"613e7f89-916e-f42e-451f-8370bdf6574b","turnId":"turn-203fd02bea1d2028380117cd4c2eb7ff","inputEntryId":"user-turn-203fd02bea1d2028380117cd4c2eb7ff-1","createdAt":1794274061496,"updatedAt":1794274061540,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, `related()` computes similarity scores against the first story and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB via boto3 rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `similar` is an empty list `[]`. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `similarity()` to return `Decimal` instead of `float`:\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\ndef similarity(a, b):\n    ...\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n```\n\nThis ensures all numeric scores stored in DynamoDB are Decimal types, which boto3 accepts.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, `related()` computes similarity scores against the first story and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB via boto3 rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `similar` is an empty list `[]`. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `similarity()` to return `Decimal` instead of `float`:\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\ndef similarity(a, b):\n    ...\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n```\n\nThis ensures all numeric scores stored in DynamoDB are Decimal types, which boto3 accepts.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-X6Ho0j/ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, `related()` computes similarity scores against the first story and stores them in the `similar` list as floats. DynamoDB via boto3 rejects float values with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `similar` is an empty list `[]`. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the first story.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `similarity()` to return `Decimal` instead of `float`:\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\ndef similarity(a, b):\n    ...\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n```\n\nThis ensures all numeric scores stored in DynamoDB are Decimal types, which boto3 accepts.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"durationMs":0.0,"approvalSource":"bypass","approvalType":"always","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"decision":"execute"}}
